(vector (map (:adr/consequences (vector "capability-based cross-org organization is validated: the vertical-capability-lib sense (:required-technology-index) already exists as structured, machine-readable data across all 175 cloud-itonami blueprints, and needed only mining + cross-referencing, not invention" "13-keyword vocabulary is small and mostly clean: 8/13 keywords resolve cleanly to a registered kotoba-lang provider; 3/13 (audit-ledger, telemetry, optimization) have no provider at all; 1/13 (cae) has an ambiguous near-miss provider; 2 providers (bpmn, dmn) have a byte-identical unregistered -clj twin left over from the ADR-2606302300 migration" "the single highest-leverage unresolved item is :audit-ledger — required by literally every one of the 175 blueprints, with no canonical named home; the real implementation is already scattered across commit-dag/prolly-tree/kotobase-peer, so this is a naming/discoverability gap, not a from-scratch build" "a much larger, purely mechanical gap was found as a side effect: all 175 cloud-itonami-* blueprint repos are unregistered in west.yml; NOT acted on here because ~80 of them (the iso3166 sub-family) are mid-flight under an active /loop maturity-promotion process (ADR-2607040800/2607042900) and a concurrent wholesale registration risks racing it" "this ADR is descriptive/analytical only: no manifest edits, no repo retirements, no new scaffolding performed. Candidate follow-ups (register kotoba-lang/identity; retire com-junkawasaki/{bpmn,dmn}-clj; batch-register the 175 cloud-itonami blueprints once the iso3166 loop is confirmed idle; scope a :supply-chain-matching capability lib) are each independent, separately-approvable pieces of work, not bundled into this ADR")), (:adr/authoritative_for (vector "disambiguation of the THREE distinct senses of \"capability\" already live in this superproject (runtime-security / labor-classification-tag / vertical-capability-lib) — see :capability-senses" "the mined :required-technology-index — 13 capability keywords used by all 175 cloud-itonami-* blueprint repos' blueprint.edn, each resolved (or flagged unresolved) against a canonical kotoba-lang provider repo" "concrete duplication finding: kotoba-lang/bpmn and kotoba-lang/dmn each have a byte-identical, unregistered, stale com-junkawasaki/{bpmn,dmn}-clj twin left over from the ADR-2606302300 migration" "concrete west-registration gap: all 175 local orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-* checkouts are unregistered in manifest/west.yml (only the private gftdcojp/cloud-itonami base repo is registered); kotoba-lang/identity (a required-technology provider used by 167/175 blueprints) is also unregistered despite being checked out" "does NOT extend the capability mining to etzhayyim (176 actors) or gftdcojp (60 products) in this pass — cloud-itonami's blueprint.edn was the only org with a uniform, machine-readable per-repo capability manifest at time of writing; etzhayyim's closest analog (:actor/labor ISIC/ISCO/UNSPSC tags) answers a different question (which human-labor vertical does this actor touch) and was not mined here" "does NOT perform any mutating action (no west registration, no repo retirement) — descriptive/analytical only, per owner instruction to do the capability-map analysis first")), (:adr/capability-senses "[{:sense :runtime-security, :aka \"object-capability / EROS-KeyKos-style access control\", :answers-the-question \"what may this RUNNING code do right now (net/fs/graph/llm-infer/...)?\", :owning-repos [\"kotoba-lang/kotoba-lang\" \"kotoba-lang/aiueos\"], :authority [\"orgs/kotoba-lang/kotoba-lang/docs/adr/ADR-safe-capability-language.md\" \"90-docs/adr/2606290930-kotoba-aiueos-capability-bridge.edn\" \"90-docs/adr/2606290900-kotoba-aiueos-key-lifecycle-revocation.edn\"], :example \"kotoba.app.edn :requires #{:cap/kqe} (etzhayyim actor mesh-deployment manifest); typed grants graph/read, net/fetch, llm/infer\", :not-for-this-adr \"irrelevant to repo/portfolio organization; this is a per-call runtime permission model, not a classification of what a repo IS\"} {:sense :labor-classification-tag, :aka \"ISIC/ISCO/UNSPSC labor-displacement accounting tag\", :answers-the-question \"which human-labor industry/occupation/product vertical does this actor's work touch (for Displacement Dividend accounting)?\", :owning-repos [\"etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-*\"], :authority [\"orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-noroshi/manifest.edn :actor/labor\"], :example \"{:isic [\\\"C26\\\" \\\"C2620\\\" \\\"J61\\\"] :isco [\\\"2152\\\" \\\"7311\\\" \\\"8212\\\"] :unspsc [\\\"32\\\" \\\"41\\\" \\\"43\\\"]}\", :not-mined-this-pass \"answers a different question (whose labor, not which tech-dependency); would need its own pass across 176 etzhayyim actors, not attempted here\"} {:sense :vertical-capability-lib, :aka \"reusable technology-capability a product/blueprint declares it depends on\", :answers-the-question \"which named, reusable kotoba-lang module implements a function this blueprint needs (banking ledger, BPMN engine, audit trail, ...)?\", :owning-repos [\"kotoba-lang/{banking,swift,phone,card,retail,logistics,property,labor,robotics,insurance,securities,bpmn,dmn,forms,identity,industry,occupation,cofog,unspsc,iso3166}\" \"cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-<code> (consumer side, via blueprint.edn :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies)\"], :authority [\"ADR-2607011000\" \"ADR-2607012000\" \"ADR-2607032000\" \"manifest/repos.edn (\\\"vertical capability lib\\\" / \\\"capability registry\\\" comments)\"], :example \"cloud-itonami-6411/blueprint.edn :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger :banking]\", :this-adr \"THIS is the sense :required-technology-index below generalizes across the whole cloud-itonami blueprint fleet\"}]"), (:adr/topic "cross-org-capability"), (:adr/related (vector "ADR-2606302300 (4-org taxonomy: what-kind-of-thing x for-whom axes; this ADR adds an ORTHOGONAL what-capability axis, does not change org placement)" "ADR-2607022800 (kotoba-lang-internal dependency map: 44 clusters + full adjacency graph; source of most canonical-provider lookups below)" "ADR-2606290930 (kotoba<->aiueos capability bridge) + ADR-safe-capability-language.md (kotoba-lang/kotoba-lang repo) — authority for the runtime-security sense of \"capability\", explicitly NOT the sense this ADR's :required-technology-index uses" "ADR-2607011000 (cloud-itonami robotics premise + ISIC-21-21 — origin of the ISIC-vertical-capability-lib pattern: swift/banking/phone/card/retail/logistics/property/labor/robotics)" "ADR-2607012000 (cloud-itonami-isco occupation blueprints), ADR-2607031600 (cofog), ADR-2607031700 (unspsc), ADR-2607032330 (iso3166), ADR-2607032000 (insurance/securities financial-services batch) — the other 4 classification-standard axes cloud-itonami blueprints are keyed on" "ADR-2607040800 + ADR-2607042900 (cloud-itonami-iso3166 maturity-promotion sweep 1 and 2, self-paced /loop) — the iso3166 sub-family is a KNOWN, actively-growing, in-progress roadmap item; this ADR's iso3166 numbers are a snapshot, not a gap report")), (:adr/status "accepted"), (:adr/id "adr-2607051300-cross-org-capability-map"), (:adr/west-registration-gap "{:cloud-itonami-blueprint-repos {:total-unregistered 175, :registered 0, :note \"manifest/west.yml has exactly one cloud-itonami-related entry: name \\\"cloud-itonami\\\", path \\\"orgs/gftdcojp/cloud-itonami\\\" — the PRIVATE business-os base repo (per ADR-2606302300's 2026-07-04 amendment). None of the 175 public cloud-itonami-<code> blueprint repos under the dedicated cloud-itonami GitHub org (per ADR-2607012100) have a west.yml entry at all.\", :scale-comparison \"35x the size of the 5-repo gap ADR-2607022800 gap-swept for kotoba-lang\", :caution \"do NOT batch-register all 175 blindly right now: the iso3166 sub-family (~80 of the 175) is mid-flight under a self-paced /loop maturity-promotion process (ADR-2607040800, ADR-2607042900) that lands its own commits in waves; a wholesale west sweep run concurrently risks racing that process. If/when this gap is closed, sequence it AFTER confirming the iso3166 loop is not currently running, and follow the same --entry-minimal-diff + server-side pin-verification discipline ADR-2607022800 used, not a wholesale regen.\"}, :kotoba-lang-identity {:total-unregistered 1, :note \"orgs/kotoba-lang/identity exists on disk, is the canonical provider for the :identity required-technology (167/175 blueprint consumers), but has zero entry in manifest/west.yml. Lower-risk, single-entry fix — no concurrent-loop conflict known.\"}}"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/required-technology-index "[{:capability :audit-ledger, :consumer-count 175, :consumer-fraction \"175/175 (universal)\", :canonical-provider nil, :status :gap, :note \"every single cloud-itonami blueprint declares this, but no kotoba-lang repo is literally named audit-ledger. The real substrate is scattered across kotoba-lang/{commit-dag,prolly-tree,kotobase-peer} + kotoba's own Datom log (ADR-2607022600 database-crates roadmap). Highest-value single fix: either register one of these as the canonical `:audit-ledger` referent in blueprint READMEs, or scaffold a thin kotoba-lang/audit-ledger contract repo that composes them, matching the pattern kotoba-lang/industry plays for :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev5.\"} {:capability :bpmn, :consumer-count 170, :consumer-fraction \"170/175\", :canonical-provider \"kotoba-lang/bpmn\", :provider-registered-in-west true, :status :duplicate-found, :note \"com-junkawasaki/bpmn-clj exists locally (untracked, unregistered), src tree BYTE-IDENTICAL (diff -rq: no differences) to kotoba-lang/bpmn. This is the ADR-2606302300 -clj-migration leftover, same shape as the kototama-clj case ADR-2607022800 Phase 5 retired. Candidate for the same retirement treatment, pending owner confirmation (not done by this ADR).\"} {:capability :forms, :consumer-count 168, :consumer-fraction \"168/175\", :canonical-provider \"kotoba-lang/forms\", :provider-registered-in-west true, :status :clean} {:capability :identity, :consumer-count 167, :consumer-fraction \"167/175\", :canonical-provider \"kotoba-lang/identity\", :provider-registered-in-west false, :status :west-registration-gap, :note \"repo exists on disk at orgs/kotoba-lang/identity but has NO entry in manifest/west.yml at all — a plain registration gap, same category as the 5 repos ADR-2607022800 gap-swept, except this one is load-bearing for 167 of 175 blueprints' declared capability layer.\"} {:capability :dmn, :consumer-count 167, :consumer-fraction \"167/175\", :canonical-provider \"kotoba-lang/dmn\", :provider-registered-in-west true, :status :duplicate-found, :note \"com-junkawasaki/dmn-clj exists locally (untracked, unregistered), src tree BYTE-IDENTICAL to kotoba-lang/dmn. Same leftover-migration shape as bpmn above.\"} {:capability :robotics, :consumer-count 80, :consumer-fraction \"80/175\", :canonical-provider \"kotoba-lang/robotics\", :provider-registered-in-west true, :status :clean, :note \"the robotics premise is explicit in every blueprint's README (\\\"a robot performs the physical domain work\\\", governor gates hardware dispatch) — matches the owner's framing that cloud-itonami is fundamentally robotics/agent-automation for supply-chain actors, not a pure SaaS form-filler.\"} {:capability :telemetry, :consumer-count 10, :consumer-fraction \"10/175\", :canonical-provider nil, :status :gap, :note \"no kotoba-lang/telemetry repo exists at all. Declared but genuinely unbuilt.\"} {:capability :insurance, :consumer-count 7, :consumer-fraction \"7/175\", :canonical-provider \"kotoba-lang/insurance\", :provider-registered-in-west true, :status :clean} {:capability :securities, :consumer-count 5, :consumer-fraction \"5/175\", :canonical-provider \"kotoba-lang/securities\", :provider-registered-in-west true, :status :clean} {:capability :banking, :consumer-count 4, :consumer-fraction \"4/175\", :canonical-provider \"kotoba-lang/banking\", :provider-registered-in-west true, :status :clean} {:capability :optimization, :consumer-count 4, :consumer-fraction \"4/175 required + 1/175 optional\", :canonical-provider nil, :status :gap, :note \"no kotoba-lang/optimization repo. Genuinely unbuilt.\"} {:capability :property, :consumer-count 2, :consumer-fraction \"2/175\", :canonical-provider \"kotoba-lang/property\", :provider-registered-in-west true, :status :clean} {:capability :cae, :consumer-count 1, :consumer-fraction \"1/175 (cloud-itonami-7210)\", :canonical-provider nil, :status :open-question, :note \"no literal kotoba-lang/cae repo. kotoba-lang/cae-solver exists and is registered, but per ADR-2607022800's naming-collision table cae-solver is \\\"reduced-order vehicle CAE solver\\\", scoped to the aero/crash/datom/echem/motor/vphysics cluster — NOT confirmed to be the same capability this one blueprint means by generic :cae. Flagged, not resolved (same discipline as ADR-2607022800's :open-questions).\"}]"), (:adr/composition-with-org-taxonomy "{:org-taxonomy-answers \"WHERE does a new repo get created? (ADR-2606302300: what-kind-of-thing x for-whom)\", :capability-map-answers \"WHAT function does an existing repo provide or consume, and who else provides/consumes the SAME function across org boundaries?\", :orthogonality \"a repo's org placement does not change; this map is a cross-cutting index layered on top, keyed by capability id, pointing at repos in whichever org actually holds them (overwhelmingly kotoba-lang for providers, per its \\\"language substrate consumed by all orgs\\\" role)\", :cloud-itonami-not-a-6th-tier \"reaffirms ADR-2606302300's 2026-07-01 amendment: cloud-itonami is not a 5th/6th taxonomy tier, it is the public-repo home for one gftdcojp product line's blueprint fleet; this ADR treats it as a CONSUMER-side data source (175 uniform blueprint.edn manifests) precisely because that fleet happens to be the only org-wide corpus with machine-readable capability declarations today\", :precedent-this-generalizes \"the ADR-2607022800 follow-up (2026-07-04) that found gftdcojp/ai-gftd-mangaka and kami-mangaka-page/render/text/scene were two unrelated things both called \\\"mangaka\\\" is exactly the class of cross-org confusion a capability-tag index is meant to make mechanically checkable instead of requiring an ad-hoc owner question each time\"}"), (:adr/last_verified "2026-07-04"), (:adr/body "# ADR-2607051300: cross-org capability map (kotoba-lang / com-junkawasaki / gftdcojp / etzhayyim / cloud-itonami)\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-04\n**Data SSoT**: `2607051300-cross-org-capability-map.edn` (this document is the\nnarrative companion; the `.edn` is the queryable source of truth)\n\n## Context\n\nFollowing ADR-2607022800 (the kotoba-lang-internal dependency map), the owner\nasked a broader question: can the dependencies/responsibilities/duplication\nacross all 5 orgs be organized along a **capability** axis, the way\n`kotoba-lang/kotoba-lang` and `aiueos` already use that word?\n\nInvestigating that question found something important before any new design\nwork was needed: **the word \"capability\" already means three different\nthings in this superproject**, and only one of them is the sense useful for\ncross-org portfolio organization. Conflating them would have produced a\nconfused schema. See `:capability-senses` in the `.edn` for the full\nbreakdown; in short:\n\n1. **Runtime-security capability** (`kotoba-lang/kotoba-lang` +\n   `kotoba-lang/aiueos`) — an object-capability / EROS-KeyKos-style\n   access-control model. Answers \"what may this *running* code do right\n   now\" (`net/fetch`, `graph/read`, `llm/infer`, ...). This is the sense\n   `ADR-safe-capability-language.md` and `ADR-2606290930-kotoba-aiueos-\n   capability-bridge` are about. **Not useful here** — it's a per-call\n   runtime permission model, not a classification of what a repo *is*.\n2. **Labor-classification tag** (etzhayyim actors' `:actor/labor {:isic\n   [...] :isco [...] :unspsc [...]}`) — which human-labor vertical an\n   actor's work touches, for Displacement Dividend accounting. Answers a\n   different question (whose labor, not which tech dependency) — not mined\n   in this pass.\n3. **Vertical capability lib** (cloud-itonami blueprints' `blueprint.edn\n   :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies`) — which named, reusable\n   kotoba-lang module implements a function a product needs. **This is the\n   sense that generalizes.**\n\nSense 3 turned out to already exist as clean, uniform, machine-readable data\nacross all 175 `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-*` blueprint repos — it just\nhadn't been mined and cross-referenced yet.\n\n## Decision\n\nMine sense 3 mechanically rather than design a new taxonomy from scratch:\n\n1. A babashka script parsed all 175 `blueprint.edn` files (0 parse errors)\n   and frequency-counted `:itonami.blueprint/required-technologies`.\n2. Each of the resulting 13 capability keywords was cross-referenced against\n   `orgs/kotoba-lang/<kw>` and `orgs/com-junkawasaki/{<kw>,<kw>-clj}` on\n   disk, then against `manifest/west.yml` registration.\n3. Any keyword resolving to both a `kotoba-lang` repo and a `-clj` sibling\n   was byte-diffed to tell genuine duplication apart from a\n   completed-but-uncleaned migration.\n\nThis ADR is **descriptive only** — no manifest edits, no repo retirements,\nno new scaffolding. Every finding below is a candidate follow-up, not an\naction already taken.\n\n## The 13-keyword capability vocabulary\n\n| capability | used by | canonical provider | west-registered | status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `:audit-ledger` | 175/175 (universal) | *none* | — | **gap** |\n| `:bpmn` | 170/175 | `kotoba-lang/bpmn` | yes | **duplicate found** |\n| `:forms` | 168/175 | `kotoba-lang/forms` | yes | clean |\n| `:identity` | 167/175 | `kotoba-lang/identity` | **no** | **west-registration gap** |\n| `:dmn` | 167/175 | `kotoba-lang/dmn` | yes | **duplicate found** |\n| `:robotics` | 80/175 | `kotoba-lang/robotics` | yes | clean |\n| `:telemetry` | 10/175 | *none* | — | **gap** |\n| `:insurance` | 7/175 | `kotoba-lang/insurance` | yes | clean |\n| `:securities` | 5/175 | `kotoba-lang/securities` | yes | clean |\n| `:banking` | 4/175 | `kotoba-lang/banking` | yes | clean |\n| `:optimization` | 4/175 | *none* | — | **gap** |\n| `:property` | 2/175 | `kotoba-lang/property` | yes | clean |\n| `:cae` | 1/175 | *ambiguous* (`cae-solver`?) | yes (solver) | **open question** |\n\n8 of 13 keywords are clean (registered, unambiguous, single provider). The\nother 5 are the actual findings:\n\n### `:audit-ledger` — the highest-leverage gap\n\nEvery one of the 175 blueprints declares this as required. No repo is\nliterally named `kotoba-lang/audit-ledger`. The real substrate already\nexists, just under other names: `commit-dag`, `prolly-tree`,\n`kotobase-peer`, and kotoba's own Datom log (ADR-2607022600's database-crates\nroadmap). This is a **discoverability gap, not a from-scratch build** — the\nfix is either naming one of these the canonical `:audit-ledger` referent, or\nscaffolding a thin composing contract repo the way `kotoba-lang/industry`\ndoes for ISIC.\n\n### `:bpmn` / `:dmn` — real, confirmed duplication\n\n`com-junkawasaki/bpmn-clj` and `com-junkawasaki/dmn-clj` both exist on disk\n(untracked, unregistered), and both have a `src/` tree that is **byte-for-\nbyte identical** to their `kotoba-lang/{bpmn,dmn}` counterparts (`diff -rq`\nreports zero differences). This is the exact shape of the `kototama-clj`\nleftover ADR-2607022800 Phase 5 retired: a completed `-clj`-suffix migration\n(ADR-2606302300) whose pre-migration original was never cleaned up. Same\nretirement treatment is the obvious follow-up, pending an explicit go-ahead\nsince it deletes a GitHub repo.\n\n### `:identity` — a plain registration gap\n\n`orgs/kotoba-lang/identity` exists on disk and is the provider 167 of 175\nblueprints declare they need, but has **zero entry in `manifest/west.yml`**.\nLower-risk than the 175-repo gap below (single entry, no known concurrent\nwork touching it).\n\n### `:telemetry` / `:optimization` — genuinely unbuilt\n\nNo `kotoba-lang` repo exists for either. Declared in blueprints, not yet\nimplemented anywhere.\n\n### `:cae` — open question, not resolved\n\n`kotoba-lang/cae-solver` exists and is registered, but ADR-2607022800's own\nnaming-collision table scopes it narrowly to \"reduced-order vehicle CAE\nsolvers\" (the aero/crash/datom/echem/motor/vphysics cluster) — not confirmed\nto be what this one blueprint (ISIC 7210, R&D natural sciences) means by\ngeneric `:cae`. Flagged, not guessed at.\n\n## The cloud-itonami blueprint fleet, as found\n\n175 local `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-*` checkouts, all real git repos\nwith a remote under the `cloud-itonami` GitHub org, all declaring\n`:itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss` and `AGPL-3.0-or-later`. Naming\nschemes: 70 plain 4-digit ISIC codes, 5 `cofog-*`, 5 `unspsc-*`, ~80\n`iso3166-*` (country/agency codes — see below), 3 `gtin-*`, and 2 oddly\ncapital-letter-prefixed (`L6810`, `M6910`).\n\nOf the 175, only **2 have graduated past scaffold to a real, actively-\ndeveloped actor**: `cloud-itonami-L6810` (real-estate agency) and\n`cloud-itonami-M6910` (Global Incorporation Actor) — both have genuine\nfeature/fix commit history, not just generated boilerplate. Empirically, the\ncapital-letter prefix correlates with \"graduated past scaffold\" rather than\nany ISIC-taxonomy convention (other ISIC Section L/M divisions in the fleet,\ne.g. 7010/7210/7320, use plain digits). Nobody has documented this on\npurpose as far as this pass found — see open questions.\n\nOne genuine small inconsistency: `cloud-itonami-L6810`'s own `blueprint.edn`\nself-identifies its `:itonami.blueprint/id` as `\"cloud-itonami-6810\"` — not\n`\"cloud-itonami-L6810\"`. Directory name, GitHub remote, and self-declared id\ndisagree. Flagged, not silently fixed, precisely because this is the fleet's\none repo with real, active development behind it.\n\n**The `iso3166-*` sub-family is not a gap** — it's a known, actively-growing\nroadmap item. ADR-2607040800 and ADR-2607042900 document two self-paced\n`/loop` sweeps that have promoted 71/193 countries + 19/19 Japan agencies\nfrom registry `:spec` to `:blueprint` so far, with 122 countries explicitly\nleft as future work. This ADR's iso3166 numbers are a snapshot, not a\nfinding.\n\n## The west-registration gap (found as a side effect, not acted on)\n\n`manifest/west.yml` has exactly **one** cloud-itonami-related entry — the\nprivate `gftdcojp/cloud-itonami` business-os base repo. **None of the 175\npublic `cloud-itonami-<code>` blueprint repos are registered at all** — 35x\nthe size of the 5-repo gap ADR-2607022800 gap-swept for kotoba-lang.\n\nThis ADR does **not** register them. Roughly 80 of the 175 (the `iso3166-*`\nfamily) are mid-flight under the self-paced `/loop` maturity-promotion\nprocess referenced above, which lands its own commits in waves — a\nconcurrent wholesale west sweep risks racing it. If/when this gap is closed,\nit should happen after confirming that loop isn't currently running, using\nthe same `--entry`-minimal-diff + server-side pin-verification discipline as\nevery other registration in this superproject, not a wholesale regen.\n\n`kotoba-lang/identity`'s single missing entry carries no such risk and could\nbe fixed independently.\n\n## Forward-looking gap: AI-driven supply-chain matching\n\nThe owner clarified mid-investigation that cloud-itonami is fundamentally\nabout **robotics/agent automation where supply-chain companies post\ninformation for AI to analyze and match** — not a plain SaaS form-filler.\nChecked for an existing capability covering this (searched kotoba-lang\nREADMEs and `repos.edn` for matching/marketplace/supply-chain terms): found\nnothing. `:robotics` (80/175 blueprints) covers the *physical execution*\npremise (a robot/actor does the domain work under a governor); there is no\nequivalent named capability yet for the *data* side — ingesting multi-party\nsupply-chain listings and running AI matching/analysis over them.\n\nThis is a genuine **forward-looking gap**, not a duplication or naming\nproblem — nothing to consolidate, something to eventually design. Candidate\nshape: a `kotoba-lang` vertical-capability-lib alongside\n`banking`/`insurance`/`securities` (e.g. `:supply-chain-matching`), consumed\nby whichever cloud-itonami blueprints need multi-party data intake —\nwholesale-trade or logistics ISIC divisions and the KAMI `:giemon` robot line\nare the most plausible first consumers. Not scoped further in this ADR; no\nrepo scaffolded.\n\n## How this composes with the existing 4-org taxonomy\n\nADR-2606302300 answers **where** a new repo gets created (what-kind-of-thing\n× for-whom). This ADR answers a different, orthogonal question: **what\nfunction** does an existing repo provide or consume, and who else provides\nor consumes the *same* function across an org boundary. A repo's org\nplacement doesn't change; the capability map is a cross-cutting index on\ntop, and it overwhelmingly points at `kotoba-lang` as provider, consistent\nwith that org's \"language substrate consumed by all orgs\" role.\n\n`cloud-itonami` is not promoted to a 6th taxonomy tier by this ADR — per\nADR-2606302300's own 2026-07-01 amendment it remains the public-repo home\nfor one `gftdcojp` product line. It's used here purely as a **data source**:\nthe only org-wide corpus with a uniform, machine-readable per-repo\ncapability manifest at the time of writing.\n\nThis generalizes exactly the kind of check ADR-2607022800's 2026-07-04\nfollow-up did by hand — discovering that `gftdcojp/ai-gftd-mangaka` and\n`kami-mangaka-page/render/text/scene` were two unrelated things both called\n\"mangaka\". A capability-tag index makes that class of cross-org confusion\nmechanically checkable instead of requiring an ad-hoc owner question each\ntime it happens to surface.\n\n## Open questions (flagged, not resolved)\n\n1. `cloud-itonami-L6810`'s self-id vs. dirname/remote mismatch — owner call\n   needed on which side is wrong, given it's the fleet's one actively-\n   developed repo.\n2. `:cae` → `cae-solver` correspondence — unconfirmed, needs the blueprint's\n   own domain context checked.\n3. Why only `L6810`/`M6910` carry a letter prefix — noted so a future\n   batch-registration pass doesn't assume a single clean regex covers all\n   175 dirs.\n\n## Follow-up (2026-07-04) — ISIC taxonomy-prefix rename, questions 1 and 3 resolved\n\nOwner instruction: normalize cloud-itonami blueprint repo names to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-{code}` / `cloud-itonami-isco-{code}` shape the ISCO\nfamily already used correctly. This closed out open questions 1 and 3 above\nand surfaced a second, larger corpus this ADR's local-checkout-only scan had\nmissed entirely.\n\n**The 175-local-checkout scan undercounted the fleet.** `gh repo list\ncloud-itonami` (the authoritative GitHub-side list) returned **288** repos,\nnot 175: 88 `cloud-itonami-isco-*` (occupation blueprints per ADR-2607012000,\nnever checked out locally, entirely absent from this ADR's original\ninventory) plus 25 more ISIC letter-prefixed repos beyond the 2 (`L6810`,\n`M6910`) this ADR had found. Combined with the 70 plain-digit + 2 sampled\nletter-prefixed repos already known, the true ISIC-family count was **97**,\nnot 2-anomalies-out-of-175. This ADR's `:cloud-itonami-blueprint-inventory`\nmaturity read (\"only L6810/M6910 graduated past scaffold\") is now known to\nhave been drawn from an incomplete sample for the same reason — the letter\nprefix was never a \"graduated\" marker (question 3's speculation), it was\nsimply this ADR's blind spot for the 25 letter-prefixed repos it never saw.\n\n**What shipped:**\n\n1. All 97 ISIC-family repos (70 plain-digit + 27 letter-prefixed) renamed on\n   GitHub via `gh repo rename` to `cloud-itonami-isic-{code}`, dropping the\n   section-letter prefix. Zero collisions, zero failures. Each repo's\n   internal self-references (`blueprint.edn`, `README.edn`, and any `docs/*`\n   file containing the old literal name) were updated and pushed in the same\n   commit as the rename.\n2. `cloud-itonami-L6810` → `cloud-itonami-isic-6810`: this also resolves\n   question 1. Its `blueprint.edn` `:itonami.blueprint/id` field had\n   pre-dated the rename disagreeing with its own dirname (self-declared\n   `\"cloud-itonami-6810\"`, no `L`) — the rename's literal-string replacement\n   pass correctly left that field alone (it never contained the string\n   `cloud-itonami-L6810`), so it was fixed with one direct follow-up edit to\n   read `\"cloud-itonami-isic-6810\"`, now agreeing with the repo name.\n3. **A previously-undiscovered coupling**: `kotoba-lang/industry`'s\n   `resources/kotoba/industry/registry.edn` (the canonical ISIC registry\n   `kotoba.industry` code reads at runtime) held `:repo`/`:business-id`\n   fields for 84 real blueprints, all pointing at the stale `gftdcojp` org\n   and, for the 12 letter-prefixed ones, a business-id that had silently\n   *dropped the letter* — e.g. the registry's \"Talent Actor\" entry (`:id\n   \"6310\"`) pointed at `gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-6310`, a URL that never\n   existed; the real repo was `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-J6310`. Confirmed\n   via `industry.cljc` that `:repo`/`:business-id` are opaque metadata\n   strings never parsed or validated (`maturity` only checks `(boolean\n   (:repo industry))`), and that `industry_test.clj` asserts exclusively by\n   ISIC `:id`, never by repo-name string — so all 84 entries were safely\n   updated to `https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-{id}` /\n   `cloud-itonami-isic-{id}` with the test suite unaffected (7 tests / 52\n   assertions green before and after).\n4. Separately found, **not fixed** (out of scope for this follow-up): of\n   `registry.edn`'s 425 entries with a non-nil `:repo`, only 84 correspond to\n   a real GitHub repo; the other **341 are phantom** — mostly (328) entries\n   explicitly tagged `:maturity :spec` that nonetheless carry a populated\n   `:repo` URL, contradicting the registry's own documented semantics\n   (`:spec` = \"registry only\", no repo yet). This is a pre-existing\n   data-integrity issue unrelated to the naming scheme and orthogonal to\n   what this ADR set out to check — recorded here for whoever next audits\n   `kotoba-lang/industry`'s registry, not resolved.\n5. Also out of scope: 13 of the 97 real repos aren't referenced with a real\n   `:maturity` tier in the registry at all (it hasn't caught up to their\n   creation) — a freshness gap, not a naming one.\n\nQuestion 2 (`:cae` → `cae-solver`) remains genuinely open; nothing in this\npass touched it.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Capability-based cross-org organization is validated: the\n  vertical-capability-lib sense already exists as structured data across\n  175 repos, and needed mining + cross-referencing, not invention.\n- 8/13 mined capability keywords are clean; the other 5 are concrete,\n  actionable findings (1 discoverability gap, 2 confirmed byte-identical\n  duplicates, 1 registration gap, 1 ambiguous naming, 2 genuinely unbuilt).\n- A much larger mechanical gap (175 unregistered west entries) surfaced as a\n  side effect and is deliberately *not* acted on here, pending confirmation\n  the concurrent iso3166 `/loop` sweep is idle.\n- This ADR bundles no action. Candidate follow-ups — register\n  `kotoba-lang/identity`; retire `com-junkawasaki/{bpmn,dmn}-clj`;\n  batch-register the 175 cloud-itonami blueprints once safe; scope a\n  `:supply-chain-matching` capability lib — are each independent and\n  separately approvable."), (:adr/follow-up-2026-07-04-isic-rename "{:trigger \"owner: \\\"cloud-itonami-isco-{code}, cloud-itonami-isic-{code} などになるようにしてね\\\"\", :corpus-size-correction {:this-adrs-original-scan 175, :actual-github-org-total 288, :gap [\"88 cloud-itonami-isco-* occupation blueprints (ADR-2607012000) — never locally checked out, entirely absent from this ADR's original :cloud-itonami-blueprint-inventory\" \"25 more ISIC letter-prefixed repos beyond the 2 (L6810/M6910) sampled locally\"], :corrected-isic-family-count 97, :invalidates \"this ADR's original maturity finding (\\\"only L6810/M6910 graduated past scaffold, letter-prefix correlates with graduation\\\") — that correlation was an artifact of an incomplete local sample, not a real pattern. The letter prefix was simply an ISIC section-letter disambiguation used inconsistently across the fleet, unrelated to maturity.\"}, :renamed {:total 97, :method \"gh repo rename, zero collisions, zero failures\", :pattern \"cloud-itonami-{code} | cloud-itonami-{SectionLetter}{code} -> cloud-itonami-isic-{code}\", :internal-refs-fixed \"blueprint.edn + README.edn + any docs/* file containing the literal old repo-name string, replaced and pushed in the same commit as each rename\", :l6810-self-id-fix \"cloud-itonami-L6810's blueprint.edn :itonami.blueprint/id already said \\\"cloud-itonami-6810\\\" (no L) BEFORE this rename -- the literal-string replacement correctly skipped it (never contained \\\"cloud-itonami-L6810\\\"); fixed with one direct follow-up edit to \\\"cloud-itonami-isic-6810\\\", now consistent\"}, :kotoba-lang-industry-registry-fix {:file \"orgs/kotoba-lang/industry/resources/kotoba/industry/registry.edn\", :finding \"84 entries (:maturity :blueprint or :implemented) had :repo/:business-id pointing at the stale gftdcojp org; 12 of those also silently dropped the ISIC section-letter, pointing at URLs that never existed (e.g. id \\\"6310\\\" -> gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-6310, real repo was cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-J6310)\", :safety-check \"industry.cljc treats :repo/:business-id as opaque metadata (maturity only checks (boolean (:repo industry))); industry_test.clj asserts exclusively by ISIC :id, never by repo-name string\", :fix \"all 84 updated to https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-{id} / cloud-itonami-isic-{id}\", :test-result \"7 tests / 52 assertions, 0 failures, before and after\", :commit \"kotoba-lang/industry@67f8dd8\"}, :found-not-fixed {:phantom-repo-entries {:count 341, :of-total 425, :note \"425 registry entries have non-nil :repo; only 84 correspond to a real GitHub repo. 328 of the 341 phantom entries are explicitly :maturity :spec (registry.cljc's own docstring: :spec means \\\"registry only\\\", no repo) yet still carry a populated :repo URL -- contradicts the registry's own documented semantics. Pre-existing, unrelated to naming, NOT fixed by this follow-up -- flagged for whoever next audits kotoba-lang/industry.\"}, :registry-freshness-gap {:count 13, :note \"13 of the 97 real ISIC-family repos aren't referenced with a real maturity tier in the registry at all yet -- registry hasn't caught up to their creation, a freshness gap not a naming one\"}, :cae-question \"question 2 (:cae -> cae-solver correspondence) untouched, remains genuinely open\"}, :superproject-side-effect {:finding \"manifest/west.yml's kami-engine pin (d432d79) was found stale/behind the local checkout + remote main (abfeb2c) while trying to push the industry fix -- the west-pin-verify-guard hook blocks ALL git push commands until this is corrected, regardless of which repo is being pushed\", :fix \"nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs --entry kami-engine, verified OK, single-line pin correction\", :unrelated-to-capability-map \"pre-existing manifest staleness, not caused by or related to the ISIC rename work; fixed only because it was blocking unrelated pushes\"}}"), (:adr/cloud-itonami-blueprint-inventory "{:total-local-dirs 175, :naming-schemes {:plain-4-digit-isic 70, :letter-prefixed-isic [\"cloud-itonami-L6810\" \"cloud-itonami-M6910\"], :cofog-coded 5, :unspsc-segment-coded 5, :iso3166-country-or-agency-coded \"~80 (see ADR-2607040800/2607042900 — actively growing family, 71/193 countries + 19/19 Japan agencies at last count)\", :gtin-family 3}, :maturity {:public-oss-scaffold-only 173, :implemented-or-actively-developed 2, :implemented-repos [{:repo \"cloud-itonami-L6810\", :isic \"6810\", :domain \"real-estate agency\", :evidence \"real git history (\\\"feat: implement Realtor-LLM ⊣ RealtorGovernor closing-execution actor\\\", operator-console HTML sample), has src/test/deps.edn unlike the scaffold-only majority, blueprint.edn carries :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented\", :anomaly \"blueprint.edn's own :itonami.blueprint/id field says \\\"cloud-itonami-6810\\\" — NOT \\\"cloud-itonami-L6810\\\" — a self-id/dirname/remote-name mismatch. Flagged in :open-questions, not fixed (this is the single most actively-developed repo in the fleet; touching its identity is exactly the kind of thing that should get an explicit owner nod first).\"} {:repo \"cloud-itonami-M6910\", :isic \"6910\", :domain \"legal/company-formation (Global Incorporation Actor)\", :evidence \"real git history (\\\"fix: :application/intake ... could fabricate a fully filed company\\\", iterative-hardening commits)\", :self-id-consistent true, :note \"unlike L6810, M6910's :itonami.blueprint/id correctly says \\\"cloud-itonami-M6910\\\" — its own dirname/remote/id all agree. The only irregularity is the capital-letter prefix itself, shared with L6810 but not explained by any ADR found; empirically it correlates with \\\"graduated past scaffold\\\" rather than any ISIC-taxonomy convention (the other ISIC Section L/M divisions in this fleet, e.g. 7010/7210/7320, use plain digits with no letter).\"}]}, :status-field \"175/175 declare :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss; :itonami.blueprint/license 175/175 AGPL-3.0-or-later\"}"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/forward-looking-gap "{:trigger \"owner clarification: cloud-itonami の本質は robotics / agent 自動化で、サプライチェーン企業が情報を載せ AI が分析・マッチングする\", :searched [\"kotoba-lang/*/README.edn for matching|marketplace|supply-chain|supply chain\" \"manifest/repos.edn for the same terms\"], :found \"zero existing repos or :required-technology keywords covering AI-driven supply-chain data intake / cross-party matching\", :interpretation \"the :robotics required-technology (80/175 blueprints) covers the PHYSICAL execution premise (a robot/actor does the domain work under a governor), but there is no equivalent named capability yet for the DATA side the owner is describing — ingesting multi-party supply-chain listings and running AI matching/analysis over them. This is a genuine forward-looking gap, not a duplication or naming problem: nothing to consolidate, something to eventually design (candidate shape: a kotoba-lang vertical-capability-lib alongside banking/insurance/securities, e.g. :supply-chain-matching, consumed by whichever cloud-itonami blueprints need multi-party data intake — ISIC divisions like wholesale trade (46xx), logistics (52xx), or the KAMI provider-split's :giemon robot line are the most plausible first consumers).\", :not-scoped-to-this-adr \"no repo scaffolded, no ADR filed for it — recorded here as a data point for whoever next works on cloud-itonami's roadmap\"}"), (:adr/method "{:step1 \"babashka script read+edn/read-string every orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-*/blueprint.edn (175 dirs, 175 files, 0 parse errors)\", :step2 \"frequency-count :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies and :optional-technologies across all 175\", :step3 \"for each keyword, test directory existence of orgs/kotoba-lang/<kw> and orgs/com-junkawasaki/{<kw>,<kw>-clj}, then grep manifest/west.yml for registration of whichever exists\", :step4 \"byte-diff any keyword resolving to BOTH a kotoba-lang repo and a com-junkawasaki -clj repo, to distinguish genuine duplication from a completed-but-uncleaned migration\", :caveat \"point-in-time snapshot (2026-07-04); does not re-run automatically; the iso3166 sub-family in particular is a known-active /loop target (ADR-2607042900) and will have moved on by the time this is read\"}"), (:adr/open-questions "[{:q \"cloud-itonami-L6810's blueprint.edn self-identifies as \\\"cloud-itonami-6810\\\", disagreeing with its own directory name and GitHub remote (cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-L6810)\", :impact \"none for west/CI today (this repo is not yet west-registered at all — see :west-registration-gap); purely a latent trap for whoever registers or renames it next\", :suggested-fix \"owner call: either rename the repo/remote to drop the stray L (matching its own self-declared id and the other 173 plain-digit-ISIC blueprints), or correct the blueprint.edn id field to match the existing L6810 name — NOT both attempted silently, since this is the fleet's only :implemented repo with real git history\"} {:q \":cae required-technology (cloud-itonami-7210) has no literal kotoba-lang/cae provider; kotoba-lang/cae-solver exists but is documented elsewhere as a different, narrower thing (reduced-order vehicle CAE solvers)\", :impact \"none currently — a single blueprint, not yet west-registered\", :suggested-fix \"confirm with the blueprint's own README/domain (ISIC 7210 = R&D natural sciences) whether it actually means kotoba-lang/cae-solver, or needs its own general-CAE capability lib\"} {:q \"why do only cloud-itonami-L6810 and -M6910 carry a capital-letter prefix, when they are also the only two blueprints that graduated past scaffold to real implementation — is the letter prefix a deliberate (if undocumented) \\\"graduated\\\" marker, an ISIC-section-letter convention applied inconsistently, or coincidental?\", :impact \"none currently (naming-only)\", :suggested-fix \"none required; noted so a future batch-registration pass does not assume all 175 dirs follow one clean regex\"}]"), (:adr/authoritative true), (:adr/scope "{:orgs-covered 5, :cloud-itonami-blueprint-dirs-scanned 175, :blueprint-edn-parsed 175, :required-technology-keywords-found 13, :duplicate-pairs-found 2, :west-registration-gaps-found 176}"), (:adr/title "ADR-2607051300: cross-org capability map (kotoba-lang / com-junkawasaki / gftdcojp / etzhayyim / cloud-itonami)"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))